end":"Rumors say a relic monster of 7 ft long inhabits Rzhev Lake. Truth or lie, folks are afraid to fish in the lake."},{"id":"marker246","name":"Fisch Monster","legend":"Rumors say a relic monster of 17 ft long inhabits Fisch Lake. Truth or lie, folks are afraid to fish in the lake."},{"id":"marker247","name":"Birwihl Monster","legend":"Tales say a relic monster of 8 ft long inhabits Birwihl Lake. Truth or lie, folks are afraid to fish in the lake."},{"id":"marker248","name":"Stapton Monster","legend":"Old sailors tell stories of a gigantic sea monster inhabiting these dangerous waters. Rumors say it can be 15 ft long."},{"id":"marker249","name":"Solis Ogre","legend":"Tales speak of a fat Ogre who inhabits Solis hills and snatches people from homes."},{"id":"marker250","name":"Lubkov Cyclops","legend":"Legends speak of a superior Cyclops who inhabits Lubkov hills and terrorizes the region."},{"id":"marker251","name":"Bicszalvalint Giant","legend":"Journeying folk speak of a terrifying Giant who inhabits Bicszalvalint hills and attacks anyone who dares to approach its lair."},{"id":"marker252","name":"Usvya Dragon","legend":"Whispers speak of a magical Dragon who inhabits Usvya hills and doesn't mind human flesh."},{"id":"marker253","name":"Testorod Cyclops","legend":"Rumors speak of a great Cyclops who inhabits Testorod hills and keeps the region at bay."},{"id":"marker254","name":"Pandos Ghoul","legend":"Inscriptions speak of a superior Ghoul who inhabits Pandos hills and prefers eating children."},{"id":"marker255","name":"Belzhets Hag","legend":"Tipplers speak of a hungry Hag who inhabits Belzhets hills and prefers eating children."},{"id":"marker256","name":"Sinca Dragon","legend":"Elders speak of a horrifying Dragon who inhabits Sinca hills and steals cattle at night."},{"id":"marker257","name":"Vovensk Hydra","legend":"Whispers speak of a magical Hydra who inhabits Vovensk hills and eats kids whole."},{"id":"marker258","name":"Oleshstiy Undead","legend":"Journeying folk speak of a horrifying Undead who inhabits Oleshstiy hills and doesn't mind human flesh."},{"id":"marker259","name":"Renaxial Hydra","legend":"Tales speak of a giant Hydra who inhabits Renaxial hills and prefers eating children."},{"id":"marker260","name":"Amazsak Troll","legend":"Whispers speak of a lucky Troll who inhabits Amazsak hills and eats kids whole."},{"id":"marker261","name":"Snenets Beast","legend":"Tipplers speak of a hungry Beast who inhabits Snenets hills and attacks unsuspecting victims."},{"id":"marker262","name":"Nichagokoe Beast","legend":"Journeying folk speak of a giant Beast who inhabits Nichagokoe hills and attacks unsuspecting victims."},{"id":"marker263","name":"Troyreumpia Ghoul","legend":"Tales speak of a proud Ghoul who inhabits Troyreumpia hills and attacks unsuspecting victims."},{"id":"marker264","name":"Dererelo Bearded Devil","legend":"Tales speak of a magical Bearded Devil who inhabits Dererelo hills and prefers eating children."},{"id":"marker265","name":"Witthengstet Dragon","legend":"Elders speak of a proud Dragon who inhabits Witthengstet hills and harasses travelers in the area."},{"id":"marker266","name":"Mstislav Ogre","legend":"Rumors speak of a horrifying Ogre who inhabits Mstislav hills and attacks unsuspecting victims."},{"id":"marker267","name":"Schonheim Forest","legend":"A forest sacred to local Word of Vorec."},{"id":"marker268","name":"Tarmouth Forest","legend":"A forest sacred to local Word of Vorec."},{"id":"marker269","name":"Bretbury Forest","legend":"A forest sacred to local Word of Vorec."},{"id":"marker270","name":"Schlutosch Forest","legend":"A forest sacred to local Word of Vorec."},{"id":"marker271","name":"Masus Forest","legend":"A forest sacred to local Word of Vorec."},{"id":"marker272","name":"Lenzgrafen Forest","legend":"A forest sacred to local Word of Vorec."},{"id":"marker273","name":"Amuroma Forest","legend":"A forest sacred to local Word of Vorec."},{"id":"marker274","name":"Ravarvia F